Spiral Waver
============

Write a function:

    def spiral_waver(size: int) -> list[list[int]]

Build a size x size matrix filled with the numbers 1 .. size*size laid out
in a clockwise spiral: start at the top-left corner, go right along the top
row, then down the right column, then left along the bottom row, then up the
left column, and keep shrinking inwards until the matrix is full. Return []
for size <= 0.

Examples:
    spiral_waver(0) -> []
    spiral_waver(-1) -> []
    spiral_waver(1) -> [[1]]
    spiral_waver(2) -> [[1, 2], [4, 3]]
    spiral_waver(3) -> [[1, 2, 3], [8, 9, 4], [7, 6, 5]]
    spiral_waver(4) -> [[1, 2, 3, 4], [12, 13, 14, 5], [11, 16, 15, 6], [10, 9, 8, 7]]
